We are a team of knowledge engineers and ontologists.

We are focused on "conceptual decomposition" to "grounded primitives". When I talk about grounded primitives here, I mean data. I'll give you an example, consider "happiness". Happiness is ontologically speaking a complex concept, because it can be modeled as an internal state, with a :feeler, and possibly some :trigger, a :duration, some :cause, etc. But here we are interested in e.g. how to individuate "happiness", and therefore we could focus on its neurophysiological manifestation, e.g. a certain facial expression, blood pressure, dopamine level etc. We want to find measurable indicators of happiness.

I have a table of features, some of them are more explicit than others, some others instead still have to be unpacked. I need you to unpack these features for me, for example if there are certain algorithm that focus on some parameters, make them explicit for me. We will start with 50 features and their descriptions.

Provide a tsv file with an additional column of "measurable indicators", when possible.